<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tatobem</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1634</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Wopigwooit</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tatobem was the grand sachem of the Pequot in the early 17th century, when the nation dominated the wampum trade of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a> and traded with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut-river">Connecticut River</a>. After a quarrel over trade at the Dutch post, the Dutch seized and killed him around 1633 or 1634. His death and the succession of his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sassacus">Sassacus</a> deepened the rivalries that led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pequot-war">Pequot War</a>.</p></div>
